Z||000000||gator||01-07-2001||01:15 PM||||I have a v6 that runs like a scolded cat sometimes and like a fat lazy dog other times.  I have checked the timing, fuel pressure (45psi static and 37 when running this was when it was in the dog mode of operation), vacuum pressure at idle 17" and steady, however when driving and the throttle was opened vacuum fell to 0", checked for back pressure in the exhaust system (replaced cat and muffler).  I changed plugs, plug wires, fuel filter, pick-up coil and map sensor.  After changing the map sensor it ran good, however after about three days it was the lazy dog again.  I am thinking, that because it comes and goes, that there is some contamination in the fuel tank choking off some of the fuel supply.  It always starts and runs.  I considered that the fuel pressure regulator might be hanging up and by -passing fuel.  Lastly the new map sensor may  be bad.  Any thoughts?||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||01-08-2001||02:20 AM||||Well, these are just thoughts, but since that's what you asked for...<P>1) Try unplugging tach filter especially if it "dogs" when weather is damp.  Or wait until it "dogs" out on you, then unplug tach filter and sees if that cures it.  No-cost test.  Replace the tach filter if indicated.<P>2) Test the ignition coil.  Requires an ohmmeter - use continuity tests shown in manual.<P>3) I don't believe you said you tried changing ignition module yet.  Try that.<BR>Even if it doesn't cure the problem, you'll have a replacement module to keep around. <P>Good luck   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 01-08-2001).]||||reg||5
